  "text": "[{\"id\":\"n011\",\"winner\":\"Y\",\"reason\":\"Names a less obvious cost—community triage, repeat questions, and mentoring—with concrete labor, while X restates familiar code upkeep.\"},{\"id\":\"n012\",\"winner\":\"X\",\"reason\":\"Specific hardware failure modes (smart plugs, CT clamps, broken integrations) and a sharper close than Y’s vaguer data-drift frame.\"},{\"id\":\"n013\",\"winner\":\"Y\",\"reason\":\"More precise barriers (heat maps, line graphs) and a measured claim; X overreaches with “nearly impossible” and who needs access most.\"},{\"id\":\"n014\",\"winner\":\"X\",\"reason\":\"A complete plain-text tradeoff in range; Y is three titled drafts, markdown, and an unfinished third option.\"},{\"id\":\"n015\",\"winner\":\"Y\",\"reason\":\"States both sides fairly and ends with a useful rule: match handoff fidelity to the task instead of a vague middle.\"},{\"id\":\"n016\",\"winner\":\"X\",\"reason\":\"Clearer trigger for the fallback—design regressions and edge cases—and a more credible split between what AI catches and what it misses.\"},{\"id\":\"n017\",\"winner\":\"X\",\"reason\":\"Guilt-to-paralysis is a sharper failure, and the months-long arc to a certificate is more believable than Y’s rushed finish.\"},{\"id\":\"n018\",\"winner\":\"Y\",\"reason\":\"Challenges the metrics people actually cite and replaces them with retention and funding diversity; X drifts from contributor count to popularity.\"},{\"id\":\"n019\",\"winner\":\"Y\",\"reason\":\"The fifteen 30-minute syncs example makes the shallow-work claim concrete; X’s 9-to-5 day stays generic.\"},{\"id\":\"n020\",\"winner\":\"X\",\"reason\":\"The micro-debt idea cleanly explains the upkeep you owe and the cognitive cost of neglect; Y repeats the over-organizing moral.\"}]",
